From: DashBerry <zero/README.md>
Subject: [PATCH] uvc: GET MAX must pair a format with one of ITS OWN frames

uvc_fill_streaming_control() computes the format range and the frame range
independently, across the whole table:

    format_last = uvc_get_frame_format_index(-1, FORMAT_INDEX_MAX);
    frame_last  = uvc_get_frame_format_index(-1, FRAME_INDEX_MAX);

then answers GET MAX with that pair. The highest format index beside the
highest frame index of ANY format is not necessarily a combination the device
offers.

On this card it never is. Measured from the daemon's own table:

    format 1 (H.264) frames 1..3   1640x922, 1920x1080, 1280x720
    format 2 (MJPEG) frames 1..2   1640x922, 1280x720

so GET MAX asks for format 2 frame 3, which does not exist — and every host
enumeration performs a GET MAX. Before the previous patch, that request landed
on an uninitialised pointer in the very next statement, which is the most
likely way the daemon was dying part-way through enumeration and taking ep0,
the console and the control port with it.

Taking each frame range within the format it will be paired with is what the
pairing meant in the first place. GET MIN was correct only by accident here
(format 1 does hold frame 1) and is fixed the same way.
---
--- a/uvc-gadget.c
+++ b/uvc-gadget.c
@@ -1405,8 +1405,20 @@
     format_first = uvc_get_frame_format_index(-1, FORMAT_INDEX_MIN);
     format_last = uvc_get_frame_format_index(-1, FORMAT_INDEX_MAX);
 
-    frame_first = uvc_get_frame_format_index(-1, FRAME_INDEX_MIN);
-    frame_last = uvc_get_frame_format_index(-1, FRAME_INDEX_MAX);
+    /* DashBerry: take the frame range WITHIN the format it will be paired
+     * with, not across the whole table.
+     *
+     * GET MAX answers (format_last, frame_last), and computed independently
+     * that is the highest format index beside the highest frame index of ANY
+     * format — a pair that need not exist. Measured on this card: H.264 is
+     * format 1 with frames 1..3, MJPEG is format 2 with frames 1..2, so GET
+     * MAX asked for format 2 frame 3. No such entry, and EVERY host
+     * enumeration performs a GET MAX.
+     *
+     * Before the previous patch, that landed on an uninitialised pointer.
+     */
+    frame_first = uvc_get_frame_format_index(format_first, FRAME_INDEX_MIN);
+    frame_last = uvc_get_frame_format_index(format_last, FRAME_INDEX_MAX);
 
     if (action == STREAM_CONTROL_MIN) {
         iformat = format_first;
